1
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:06,300
- Hey. - Hi.

2
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:09,000
Pheebs, what's wrong?

3
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:11,340
I'm just so exhausted from dragging around

4
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:13,040
this huge engagement ring.

5
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:14,654
Oh, my God.

6
00:00:14,674 --> 00:00:15,974
Congratulations.

7
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:17,900
So did he get on one knee?

8
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,420
Did he have a speech prepared?

9
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:20,780
Oh, did he cry?

10
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:25,420
Yeah, big surprise, I like proposals.

11
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:29,180
Well, it was really sweet,

12
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:31,280
and, like, the most romantic thing ever.

13
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:33,080
Here's to Phoebe,

14
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:34,980
who's found the greatest guy in the world.

15
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:36,280
To Phoebe and--

16
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:37,680
I want to say "Mike"?

17
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:40,440
To Phoebe and Mike.

18
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:42,400
Thank you.

19
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:44,440
Oh, and I have something for you.

20
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,480
It's my little black book.

21
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:48,260
It's got the numbers of all the guys I've dated.

22
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,720
Oh, Phoebe, that's nice,

23
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:53,100
but you know what? I think I'm okay.

24
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:53,740
Why don't you just give it

25
00:00:53,740 --> 00:00:55,140
to one of your other single girlfriends.

26
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:56,900
I would, but you're the last one.

27
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:00,400
Give me the book!

28
00:01:02,833 --> 00:01:04,603
"Pablo Diaz.

29
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:06,380
Brady Smith.

30
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:08,920
Guy in Van"?

31
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:10,500
Oh, my first love.

32
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:14,420
What is the red X next to

33
00:01:14,420 --> 00:01:15,700
Bob Gremore's name mean?

34
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:16,480
Dead.

35
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:21,920
Oh, it's okay. No, he was old. Yeah.

36
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:23,620
And he lived a full life.

37
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:25,600
He was in the first wave at Omaha Beach.

38
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:25,980
Omaha Beach:1944年诺曼底登陆中美军负责的一段

39
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:29,520
oh, I'm sorry. I should've given you guys my black book

40
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:30,380
when I got married.

41
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:31,880
Although, it wasn't so much a book

42
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:32,920
as a napkin.

43
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,840
With Janice's phone number on it.

44
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:40,660
Phoebe, isn't Jethro Tull a band?

45
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:46,280
Oh, yes, they are.

46
00:01:48,495 --> 00:01:50,725
《老友记》第十季第六集 罗斯的科研补助金

47
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:28,720
Hey, honey.

48
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:31,140
Hey, sweetie.

49
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:34,140
- Is Monica not here? - No.

50
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:35,420
Then I'll tell you.

51
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:38,260
My agency was bidding for a big account, and they got it.

52
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:40,000
It's my first national commercial.

53
00:02:40,140 --> 00:02:40,760
Cool.

54
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:41,860
And I don't want to brag,

55
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:43,300
but a lot of the ideas were mine.

56
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:45,260
Hell, you weren't there.

57
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:46,620
All the ideas were mine.

58
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:48,660
That's great.

59
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:51,080
Hey, can you cast me in it?

60
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:54,120
I really don't think you're right for the part.

61
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:55,820
What do you mean? I can do anything.

62
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:56,700
I'm a chameleon.

63
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:00,360
I'm old.

64
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:04,100
I'm tired.

65
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:07,340
Oh, I am hot. I'm cold.

66
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:09,340
Come on, what can't I do?

67
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:12,740
First of all, bravo.

68
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:15,740
But I don't think you're right for this.

69
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:18,060
The part's a stuffy college professor.

70
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:19,560
I can do that.

71
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:21,880
Hello, I'm your professor.

72
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:24,580
When I'm not busy thinking of important things,

73
00:03:24,580 --> 00:03:26,600
or professing...

74
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:30,240
...l like to use-- What's the product?

75
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:33,720
Software that facilitates inter-business networking e-solutions.

76
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:40,440
I'm cold.

77
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:44,620
- Hey. - Hey.

78
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:45,980
Guess who's a finalist

79
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:47,940
for a huge research grant?

80
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:48,720
I'll give you a hint.

81
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:49,940
He's looking right at you.

82
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:53,200
Well, unless it's the creepy guy

83
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,260
with his hand up his kilt...

84
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:56,160
...I'm gonna say, "Congratulations."

85
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:58,760
I'm so excited.

86
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:02,100
Apparently, I beat out hundreds of other applicants...

87
00:04:02,340 --> 00:04:04,900
...including five guys I went to graduate school with.

88
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,680
Not that I'm keeping score, or anything. Five.

89
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:10,680
- Wow, that's great. - Yeah.

90
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:11,720
So tell me about the grant.

91
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:13,920
Well, okay, it's for $25,000.

92
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:14,780
And if I get it,

93
00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:17,320
I'll be able to complete my field research.

94
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:19,520
And there will be an article about me

95
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:21,440
in the <i>Paleontology Review</i>.

96
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:23,700
It'll be the first time my name is in there...

97
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:26,020
...without people raising serious questions about my work.

98
00:04:28,620 --> 00:04:29,980
Are you talking about the Dewer Grant?

99
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:30,920
Yeah. Why?

100
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:33,200
Benjamin Hobart is administering that grant.

101
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:35,500
- Your ex-boyfriend? - Yeah.

102
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:38,180
So your ex-boyfriend is gonna determine

103
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:40,180
if your new boyfriend gets this grant?

104
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:41,780
Wow, your new boyfriend is screwed.

105
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:45,940
No. No, we ended on great terms.

106
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:46,600
I mean if anything,

107
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:48,900
I think this could help you. You know what?

108
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:50,020
Why don't we all go out to dinner,

109
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:51,480
and I can introduce you.

110
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,180
If you think it'd help.

111
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:54,880
Yeah, absolutely. I'll call him.

112
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,980
Now, is there anything I could do to butter him up?

113
00:04:58,260 --> 00:04:59,380
Anything he really likes?

114
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:03,200
He does have a pretty serious latex fetish.

115
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:04,440
We'll see how dinner goes.

116
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,740
- Hey. - Hey, you want to go see a movie?

117
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:15,360
I told you I had to spend all day clearing out stuff

118
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,420
so Mike could move in.

119
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:17,860
- Oh, right. - Yeah.

120
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:20,100
Now that I'm here,

121
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:22,080
I might as well help with the cleaning and organizing.

122
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:24,580
I just happen to have my label maker.

123
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:29,180
Oh, it's so hard to get rid of stuff.

124
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:31,500
Did you and Chandler make compromises

125
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:32,720
when you moved in together?

126
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:33,800
Chandler did.

127
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:36,840
What does he want you to give up?

128
00:05:36,940 --> 00:05:38,160
A bunch of stuff.

129
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:39,520
And the worst one,

130
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:41,200
he wants me to get rid of Gladys.

131
00:05:41,900 --> 00:05:42,580
Who's Gladys?

132
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:49,080
What a tragic loss.

133
00:05:50,540 --> 00:05:52,180
Yeah, I really hate to give her up.

134
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:54,720
Oh, I know. Oh, you should take her.

135
00:05:58,500 --> 00:05:59,840
I don't know.

136
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:02,240
What, you don't like her?

137
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:05,860
Of course I do. What's not to like?

138
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:08,280
I'd take her in a minute.

139
00:06:10,020 --> 00:06:11,880
But I think that you're giving up too easy.

140
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:13,940
Honey, I think that you need to fight for her.

141
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:17,420
- Really, you think? - Absolutely.

142
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:18,640
You say to him,

143
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:20,920
"I'm sorry, Mike, I can't live without her.

144
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:22,500
She means too much to me."

145
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:26,140
Okay, I'll fight for her. Okay.

146
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:29,360
Oh, wait. I just realized, if I do that,

147
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:30,380
that means you don't get her.

148
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,440
Damn it, I did not think this through.

149
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:37,520
- Hey, guys. - Hey.

150
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:40,460
Oh, any word on casting yet?

151
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:42,620
I told you, you're not right for the part.

152
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:43,640
What do you mean?

153
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:45,500
Rach, don't I seem like a professor

154
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:47,260
you'd buy some kind of e-crap from?

155
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:49,820
I'm sorry,

156
00:06:49,820 --> 00:06:51,980
this sounds like something I'm never gonna be interested in.

157
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,740
Look, come on, please?

158
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,680
It's not like I'm asking you for some crazy favor.

159
00:06:57,940 --> 00:06:59,200
This is what I do for a living.

160
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:00,760
I am a professional actor.

161
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:02,960
Man, I'm two hours late for work.

162
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:06,300
Here's a copy of my reel.

163
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:08,000
It's got all the commercials that I've been in.

164
00:07:08,340 --> 00:07:09,920
- Joe-- - Just watch it.

165
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:11,060
If you don't like it,

166
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,660
don't pass it on to your bosses.

167
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:15,020
- Fine. - Thank you.

168
00:07:19,797 --> 00:07:22,187
- Work, Joe. - Damn it.

169
00:07:26,060 --> 00:07:27,180
What am I gonna do now?

170
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:28,620
Just pass the tape along.

171
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:30,220
He's not right for the part.

172
00:07:30,420 --> 00:07:31,040
If I suggest him,

173
00:07:31,060 --> 00:07:32,720
my bosses will think I'm an idiot.

174
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:34,900
And that's something they should learn on their own.

175
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:38,380
Just tell Joey that you watched the tape...

176
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:40,160
...and you liked it, but your bosses didn't.

177
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:41,940
Then that way, you're the good guy,

178
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:42,820
and they're the bad guy.

179
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:45,080
That's good. I liked it, they didn't.

180
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:50,280
Joey, for God's sake, go to work.

181
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:58,900
I can't believe I'm about to meet Benjamin Hobart.

182
00:07:59,040 --> 00:08:01,260
I've always thought of him as someone I'd invite...

183
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:03,020
...to my fantasy dinner party.

184
00:08:04,780 --> 00:08:06,140
Do you think there's any chance

185
00:08:06,140 --> 00:08:08,020
he'll bring Christie Brinkley or C-3PO?

186
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:11,920
Sorry, it looks like it's just him.

187
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:15,500
Charlie.

188
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:21,640
My God, you look absolutely stunning.

189
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:24,940
Well, I am having a good hair day.

190
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:29,180
- It's so good to see you. - Oh, you too.

191
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:34,480
I'm okay.

192
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:39,260
I'm sorry. Ross Geller, Benjamin Hobart.

193
00:08:39,660 --> 00:08:41,060
It's an honor to meet you.

194
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:42,920
I can't tell you how long...

195
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:46,520
...I've been an admirer of your work. I mean, that Nobel Prize.

196
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:50,880
I mean, I have to tell you

197
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:53,380
that you're one of the reasons I got into the field.

198
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:55,560
Well, likewise.

199
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:58,300
Actually not likewise.

200
00:08:58,420 --> 00:08:59,780
I'd never heard of you until this morning.

201
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:01,380
But it's nice to be nice.

202
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,300
- Shall we? - Yeah. Thank you.

203
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:12,760
I can't believe that you chose this restaurant.

204
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:14,780
Do you remember the night?

205
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:17,540
Oh, my God. I completely forgot.

206
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:22,060
Oh, my God, I can't believe they let us back in this place.

207
00:09:30,381 --> 00:09:31,821
You weren't there.

208
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:36,500
No, but, you know, it's just a funny image.

209
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:39,620
You know, the two of you in this restaurant with the....

210
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:45,640
Ross, why don't you tell Benji

211
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:47,420
about your proposal while I go to the ladies' room.

212
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:52,260
So tell me about it.

213
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:56,730
Painted Desert:在亚利桑那州北部

214
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:56,240
Okay. Well, I would like to do a dig in the Painted Desert.

215
00:09:57,240 --> 00:10:00,360
There are still several areas that haven't been fully excavated.

216
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,620
- Break up with Charlie. - What?

217
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:02,620
What?

218
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:08,800
Did you just say, "Break up with Charlie"?

219
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:11,220
Well, yes and no.

220
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:14,200
Yes, I did say it. And no, I didn't not say it.

221
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:17,740
Kind of inappropriate, don't you think?

222
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:20,060
Listen, I'm sorry.

223
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:21,580
I just haven't seen her for so long,

224
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:23,440
all these feelings are rushing back.

225
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:24,460
I'm starting to realize

226
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:26,280
how much I've missed her.

227
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:29,320
And I'm gonna need you to break up with her.

228
00:10:31,060 --> 00:10:32,160
Are you serious?

229
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:33,660
If you say, yes, then I'm serious.

230
00:10:33,680 --> 00:10:34,920
If you say, no, then I'm joking.

231
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:39,060
- No. - Joking it is.

232
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:44,820
Hi, sorry I'm late.

233
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:46,280
Hey, how'd it go with Mike?

234
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:47,600
Is he gonna let you keep the painting?

235
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:50,000
No, he really hates it.

236
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:52,980
But he's gonna let me keep my box of human hair.

237
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:56,300
So you gotta pick your battles.

238
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:59,520
But the good news is, Gladys is yours.

239
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:03,240
Wow, what's the bad news?

240
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:05,740
Who's Gladys?

241
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:07,940
Oh, she's that work of art I made.

242
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:09,640
You know, with the woman coming out of the frame.

243
00:11:11,980 --> 00:11:14,560
And Monica gets to keep her?

244
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:18,600
In her house? I am so jealous.

245
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:22,940
I didn't know you wanted her too.

246
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:27,220
Well, I mean, sure, of course.

247
00:11:28,340 --> 00:11:30,980
But you already gave that to Monica, so....

248
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,400
You know, I would give her up for you.

249
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:34,980
No, I couldn't let you do that.

250
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:37,500
- No, but I want to. - But I don't want you to.

251
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:41,260
- But I insist. - But I insist harder.

252
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:45,760
Girls. Girls. Stop. Okay, we'll flip a coin.

253
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,000
Heads, she's Rachel's.

254
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,140
Tails, she's Monica's.

255
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:53,000
Tails. Monica, she's yours.

256
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:54,880
No, that landed in your food.

257
00:11:56,640 --> 00:11:57,500
No, no, that's okay.

258
00:11:57,560 --> 00:11:59,480
You won fair and square. I'm so sad.

259
00:12:03,900 --> 00:12:04,660
Hey, Joe?

260
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:06,520
- What's up? - Bad news.

261
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:07,600
I watched the tape

262
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:08,900
and passed it along to my bosses

263
00:12:08,980 --> 00:12:09,920
and they weren't interested.

264
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:13,700
I'm sorry, man.

265
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:18,020
But you watched the tape?

266
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:20,800
Yeah, I liked it.

267
